WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.426
The workbook sorts every
asset into coverage tiers,

2
00:00:03.426 --> 00:00:05.938
and Ansible's job changes with the tier.

3
00:00:05.938 --> 00:00:09.838
In tier one it onboards and reads,
but it doesn't own settings.

4
00:00:09.838 --> 00:00:15.467
Tier two is its natural home: it owns
configuration where the C M D B says so,

5
00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:18.563
and every job's result becomes evidence.

6
00:00:18.563 --> 00:00:22.812
In tier three it only reads, and in
tier four it does nothing at all.

7
00:00:22.812 --> 00:00:26.312
Of the workbook's four
tracks, Ansible lives in two.

8
00:00:26.312 --> 00:00:28.374
The Arc track, for servers.

9
00:00:28.374 --> 00:00:31.994
And the non-person identity
track, because the controller

10
00:00:31.994 --> 00:00:35.537
itself is an identity with
standing access to many hosts.

11
00:00:35.537 --> 00:00:37.300
Let's start with the Arc job.
